<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Al Khairat brings unique benefits compared to other thermal power plants in Iraq:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list --><ul><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Largest in Iraq: When fully operational, it will supply over 10% of the country’s electricity needs.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Efficient Fuel Use: Reduces dependency on natural gas by utilizing heavy fuel oil and crude oil.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Environmental Compliance: Equipped with advanced systems to minimize emissions and pollution, such as:</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Air Quality Control System meeting WB/IFC standards for NOx, SOx, and dust emissions.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Emission Monitoring System for real-time tracking.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Zero Liquid Discharge Wastewater Treatment, enabling water recycling.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Additionally, Al Khairat plans to conserve water resources by using treated water from the Karbala Wastewater Treatment Plant.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->
